      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Sixteen angina patients were submitted to echocardiographic examination during the cold pressor test and during hand grip. Certain left ventricular function echocardiographic parameters were assessed in these subjects and in a further 14 patients presenting negative histories for cardiovascular diseases who represented the control group. Of the two tests associated with echocardiography, the cold pressor test appeared capable of inducing the more evident changes on left ventricular function compared to isometric effort in subjects suffering from ischaemic cardiopathy."},
